    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0262" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.21/220.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Harrison to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-09T17:00:00-04:56">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have seen the Minister for Foreign Affairs by appointment to receive Colombia’s
                    reply to the proposition of your December 19, 6 p.m.<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d148-f1"/> The Minister apologized for the delay in answering, due
                    to unavoidable absence of one of the members of the Consultatory Commission of
                    the Foreign Office. He hopes to have a reply for me by the 13th instant.* * *
                    Our negotiations are, in fact, not with the Government but with the
                    Commissioners, representing all political parties, with whom the Government has
                    but little influence.* * *</p>
                <p>Any concession the Department may be able to grant would go far toward a
                    settlement. If, however, the Department cannot accept their draft,<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d148-f2"/> a full frank explanation of the reasons therefor would
                    undoubtedly have a beneficial effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
